    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class configured in this project). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the Owner response following the existing pattern for computed read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the field in `toOwnerDto` via `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` and added a small single-responsibility helper:\n\n   ```java\n   default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n       boolean noNamesakes = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount());\n       boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n       return noNamesakes && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe logic returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE` \u2014 matching the spec. The helper is null-safe on both `namesakeCount` and `email`. Both acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full build pass green.",
